This Python script builds a neural network to predict customer churn using TensorFlow.

Data Preprocessing:

The dataset (Churn_Modelling.csv) is loaded, and the independent variables (X) and target variable (y) are separated.

Categorical variables (Gender, Geography) are encoded using LabelEncoder and OneHotEncoder.

Data Splitting and Scaling:

The data is split into training and testing sets (80%/20%).

Features are standardized using StandardScaler.

Model Building:

A neural network with two hidden layers (6 units each, ReLU activation) and an output layer (sigmoid activation) is created.

Training and Evaluation:

The model is trained for 100 epochs, then predictions are made on the test set.

Accuracy and the confusion matrix are printed to evaluate the model.

New Customer Prediction:

The model predicts whether a new customer will stay or leave based on preprocessed input data.

In summary, the script preprocesses the data, builds and trains a neural network, evaluates its performance, and makes predictions for new customers.
